coins.clueText:
INT stores whole numbers: int score = 10;

DOUBLE stores decimal numbers: double price = 19.99;

Clue: Some values are whole, while others continue beyond the decimal point.

BOOLEAN stores one of two values: true or false.

Example: boolean isOpen = true;

Clue: Some information has only two possible states.

STRING stores text or a sequence of characters.

Example: String name = "Java";

Clue: Numbers, truth, and words may all be stored, but Java must know what kind of value each one represents.

